The log's entries for a kit buff the replay can't judge, matched only against the engine's modifiers of the same game
buff (enginecheck.ts loggedEntries). HELD BACK, NOT DROPPED: a fix in the check, which another agent held during the
damage-factors round (2026-11-26); for the lead to apply.

The bug: loggedEntries drops a listed entry of an unjudged kit buff (its state is the log's: Ember's Pay the Ferric
Price, on `attacked`) when any judged engine modifier has the same zone and a near value, whatever buff it is. In 7e19
from 25 s Ember's talent-2 ATK +0.09 was swallowed by one of Pogranichnik's two Thermite Cutter layers (+0.09 ATK
each), so her primary reading had neither: her 25.81 s slam ×1.094 is that ATK plus Fervent Morale at its boundary
(+0.17 ATK%, exactly), and 0c14's Alesh P3 (+0.15) the same way.

Measured (2026-11-26, `npm run measure -- --at HEAD --patch <this> --hits`, at c509b8f): development plain 69.0%
unchanged (c4f3 mismatch 53 → 52; a9d7 assumed +9, fallback −9), hold-out plain 79.0 → 80.4%, mismatch 5.9 → 5.6%,
mean |damage error| 8.5 → 8.4% (3 better, 0 worse), earlier pending 0c14 −4.9 → −3.4%, 7e19 mismatch 7 → 4.

diff --git a/packages/logs/src/enginecheck.ts b/packages/logs/src/enginecheck.ts
index f3cc541..0f7cb70 100644
--- a/packages/logs/src/enginecheck.ts
+++ b/packages/logs/src/enginecheck.ts
@@ -174,7 +174,7 @@ export function loggedEntries(c: EngineCheck, effects: readonly LogEffect[], gam
   const out: LogEffect[] = [];
   for (const e of effects) {
     if (!gameBuffs.has(e.buff)) continue;
-    const i = pool.findIndex((m) => m.zone === e.zone && (m.element ?? null) === (e.element ?? null) && near(m.value, e.value));
+    const i = pool.findIndex((m) => m.zone === e.zone && (m.element ?? null) === (e.element ?? null) && near(m.value, e.value) && m.kitBuff !== undefined && (c.names.ofKitBuff.get(`${m.kitBuff.owner}:${m.kitBuff.id}`) ?? []).includes(e.buff));
     if (i >= 0) pool.splice(i, 1);
     else out.push(e);
   }
